    <string name="compress_audio">Slow connection: upload OGG/Opus</string>
    <string name="compress_audio_hint" formatted="false">On: uploads are ~10x smaller (OGG/Opus) but the phone spends ~8 % of the audio length encoding before each request — that delay is part of the stop wait. Off: WAV, no encode cost. Live transcription runs either way.</string>
    <string name="advanced_section">Advanced / seldom needed</string>
    <string name="slice_auto">Fragment cut: auto</string>
    <string name="slice_seconds">Fragment cut (slice) in seconds</string>
    <string name="slice_seconds_hint" formatted="false">The slice is a fragment\'s MAXIMUM length. The cut is searched in the last part of the slice, so a fragment ends up between (100 − search window) % and 100 % of it. Auto measures your STT provider\'s latency and picks the largest slice whose stop wait stays within budget — bigger slices mean fewer seams. Manual: 5–180 s.</string>
    <string name="slice_seconds_error">Enter a fragment cut between 5 and 180 seconds, or switch auto on</string>
    <string name="search_percent_auto">Search window: auto</string>
    <string name="search_percent" formatted="false">Search window in % of the slice</string>
    <string name="search_percent_hint" formatted="false">The last N % of the slice is the only region where a cut may land — it is where the app looks for a pause. Auto keeps it as small as possible while almost every seam still finds a silence. Manual: 10–60 %.</string>
    <string name="search_percent_error" formatted="false">Enter a search window between 10 and 60 %, or switch auto on</string>
    <string name="audio_evidence">Keep session audio for diagnostics</string>
    <string name="audio_evidence_hint">Dictated audio is retained locally for diagnostics: the actually-uploaded fragments plus a session.json manifest (timestamps, statistics, transcripts, delivery) under files/audio, adb-readable. The slider sets how long — from no retention (nothing is written) up to 50 years. Storage pressure evicts the oldest sessions invisibly.</string>
